  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 220
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "start",
        "title": "On the cushion cart",
        "description": "This scene opens the game and the story: the prologue on the road into Caerwyn. Open on the cart: the cushions, the amber light, the crossroads coming up, Fitch grumbling and Tansy's questions. Give the player a moment to be someone (Tansy asks who they are and why they're going to the Assembly; Fitch asks whether they can use whatever they carry), two or three exchanges at most, and then the goblins. Keep it light and quick: this is the calm before the arrow. Don't explain the world; let Fitch and Tansy show it (the Assembly in two days, the King who ordered cushions himself, a road with no patrols, 'lost to goblins'). The opening image: three hundred green cushions on a cart in the low sun, a girl on top of them, the hedges black ahead.",
        "cast": {
          "fitch": "Characterise: up front with the reins, grumbling about the road, the light and the King's cushions, and watching the hedges. Gives the player a job if they've nothing to do ('Keep your eyes on that hedge, friend'). Hooks: the patrol that's meant to meet them at Garrow's bridge, a mile on.",
          "tansy": "Characterise: up top on the cushions, questions for the player one after another: who they are, why they're going to the Assembly, whether they've seen the King, how they take their tea (the King remembers everybody's, Grandad says). She's the first to see the hedge move.",
          "nabber": "Not here yet: in the hedges, waiting. Nothing is said of them before the ambush, though the hedge can rustle once."
        },
        "lore": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ambush",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 420,
        "y": 220
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "beat",
        "title": "Goblins in the hedge",
        "description": "An arrow thumps into the cushions a hand's breadth from Tansy, and the hedges burst: goblins out through the gaps on both sides of the road, shrieking 'Be seen! Be seen!', one with a bow up the road ahead, Bramble rearing in the shafts. It's played on the board, a turn each in initiative order: Nabber's hedge-gang against the player, Fitch beside them with his cudgel, Tansy under the cushions (she never fights). The goblins would sooner frighten than fight: hurt, or seeing two of their own drop, a goblin breaks for the gaps and away east toward the bridge. More of the gang may come up the road behind the cart once it's started. When it's over the scene picks up from how it went: the cart, the cushions, Fitch and Tansy, the fallen goblins and what's on them, and smoke over the bridge.",
        "cast": {
          "nabber": "Out of the gaps in the hedges shrieking 'Be seen!', the bow shooting at the cart from up the road; they go for whoever's nearest and loudest, and the horse. Hurt, or with two of their own down, they break and run east for the bridge. One held down begs and tells.",
          "fitch": "Stands up on the cart bellowing at them like a sergeant, then gets down beside the player with his cudgel; puts himself between the goblins and Tansy every time.",
          "tansy": "Under the cushions at the first arrow, as she was told; peeks out to shout warnings ('Behind you!'); never fights."
        },
        "pressure": "The light is going and there's smoke over the river ahead: Fitch wants the cart moving and the patrol found before dark, says so, and then gets the cart moving himself.",
        "fight": {
          "foes": [
            "nabber",
            "goblin-blade",
            "goblin-bow"
          ],
          "allies": [
            "fitch"
          ]
        },
        "lore": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "be-seen",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 840,
        "y": 40
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "beat",
        "title": "Paid to be seen",
        "description": "The player comes to see that the goblins weren't after the cart or the cushions: they were making a show on the road, for pay. It's a first glimpse of the story's heart (the 'lost' grain wagons), and nobody here understands it yet: let it puzzle them. It can only come out once the fight has begun.",
        "revelation": "The goblins weren't after the cart or the cushions: they were paid to make a show on the road ('Be seen!'), in new silver heron pennies nobody out here has ever seen, by someone they call Longlegs.",
        "paths": [
          {
            "via": "the goblins' pouches",
            "clue": "Every goblin that's fallen, dead or out cold, has a few new silver pennies in the pouch round its neck, stamped with a heron: good silver, new this month, money nobody in the Nine Furrows has ever seen (Fitch hasn't).",
            "earn": "No dice: free to anyone who searches a fallen goblin.",
            "strength": "suggestive"
          },
          {
            "via": "nabber",
            "clue": "A goblin held down and offered its life: 'Longlegs pays! Be seen on the road, shoot the cows, run away! Shiny pennies!' Longlegs is a tall one in a grey hood who smells like flowers. That's all it knows, and it'll say anything to be let go.",
            "earn": "No dice: for a goblin that's beaten, held and offered its life. Threatened instead, it squeals it faster, or lies; that's the roll.",
            "strength": "suggestive",
            "check": {
              "skill": "intimidation",
              "dc": 10
            }
          },
          {
            "via": "fitch",
            "clue": "Forty years on this road, and he has never seen a goblin carry off so much as a sack of grain: they shoot the oxen and run. 'Lost to goblins,' the city says of the palace's grain wagons. Lost where? What would a goblin do with a wagon of wheat?",
            "earn": "No dice: once the fight's over and he's had a pull at his flask, or when asked what goblins want.",
            "strength": "hook"
          },
          {
            "via": "tansy",
            "clue": "She heard them shouting it: 'Be seen! Be seen!' 'Why would they want to be seen? I'd want to be hidden, actually, if I was a goblin.'",
            "earn": "No dice: she says it as soon as she's out from under the cushions.",
            "strength": "hook"
          }
        ],
        "establishes": [
          "paid-to-be-seen"
        ],
        "lore": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "the-bridge",
      "type": "story",
      "position": {
        "x": 840,
        "y": 260
      },
      "data": {
        "kind": "beat",
        "title": "Smoke at the bridge",
        "description": "The player learns where the trouble really is, and where the road goes on: the toll bridge a mile ahead, where the goblins' war-band has the King's patrol pinned. This is the lead to the next scene, so the player must have it before the scene can end well; it comes out only once the fight has begun, and the smoke is free to anyone who looks east.",
        "revelation": "The goblins came from Garrow's toll bridge a mile on, where the rest of their band and a war-boss have the King's patrol pinned down; smoke is going up over the river, and the cart's only way into the city is across that bridge.",
        "paths": [
          {
            "via": "tansy",
            "clue": "Back up on the cushions, Tansy sees it first: black smoke going up over the river ahead, and a horn, far off. 'That's where the soldiers are! Grandad said there'd be soldiers at the bridge!'",
            "earn": "No dice: once the fight's done and she has climbed back up (she always climbs back up).",
            "strength": "strong"
          },
          {
            "via": "fitch",
            "clue": "The palace sent word that the one patrol on the road this week would meet the King's cushions at Garrow's bridge, a mile on. That smoke is the bridge, and he doesn't like it.",
            "earn": "No dice: once the goblins are gone and he sees the smoke, or is asked where help is.",
            "strength": "strong"
          },
          {
            "via": "nabber",
            "clue": "A goblin begging for its life squeals that the boss is at the bridge with the big band and his worg, 'pinning the shiny-hats' (the soldiers), and they were only to keep the crossroads.",
            "earn": "No dice: from a goblin that's beaten and held; it wants to be let go to run to its boss.",
            "strength": "strong"
          },
          {
            "via": "the smoke",
            "clue": "Black smoke going up over the trees to the east, where the road meets the river, and the far-off bray of a horn: someone's in trouble at the bridge.",
            "earn": "No dice: free to anyone who looks east once the fight is over.",
            "strength": "suggestive"
          }
        ],
        "required": true,
        "establishes": [
          "trouble-at-bridge"
        ],
        "lore": []
      }
    },
